LOK: Calc reads and writes one cell by address, the cursor kept

- .uno:CellAt?address=Sheet1!A1 reads one cell: its absolute address,
  the text shown and the input (a formula as typed). The sheet must be
  named and exist; otherwise the answer is {"error": "address"}.
- .uno:EnterString takes Address: the string goes into that cell on its
  own sheet, one undo step; the cursor, the selection and the selected
  sheets stay. ScViewFunc::EnterData wrote into every selected sheet.
  The current cell's input line follows such a write.
  Another program edits an open workbook this way (Ely #19).
- Text with a line break entered as a string records its undo step
  (SetEditCell); it went in through SetEditText with none.

